** Last Change: Sun Nov 30 19:48:13 1997
*/

Purpose:

    This utility allows you to have a web page display the finger information
of users on your system.

Requirments:

    A TCP stack (AmiTCP or Miami preferrable)
    A web server (AWS preferred, but it will work it apache as well if you make
      an AWS: assign to accomodate the placement of the conf file)
    CNet/4 (any version after 4.13)

Features:

    Simple to install and configure.
    Will do a finger lookup on Handle, Mail ID, Account #, or real name (if not
      marked as private).
    Shows if the user is online or not (also says they aren't if they are hiding).
    Shows if the user has any new email waiting for them.

Installation:

    Installation of finger-cgi is simple.  Just copy the executable in the
archive to the appropriate place in your AWS: directory (cgi-bin suggested).

    Tada!  It's installed.

Usage:

    Just use any web browser to access http://your.site.com/cgi-bin/finger
To specify a user to finger, call it as
http://your.site.com/cgi-bin/finger?<HANDLE|MAILID|REALNAME|ACC#>
    If you have the files AWS:conf/finger.head and AWS:conf/finger.foot, they
will be used as a header and footer, respectively.  The contents of these files
is just your normal HTML commands.

